{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791042248,"nonce":"ImaY6s1skOnM2EbtDOB85G255sE=","title":"Hit testing ignores clip-path","message":"An element with Prop.ClipPath is drawn clipped to its shape (circle, ellipse, inset, rect, xywh), but blinc_abi's hit test (hit.rs) only knows rect clips, so a press on a corner a circle clips away still hits the element and its children. The hit test should resolve the innermost clip-path along the path the same way display_list's shape_clip does (in the element's own coordinates, through its transform) and skip points outside it. Reproducer: a 40x40 div with clipPath={ClipPath.circle()} and an onClick; Pointer.press/release at (2, 2) inside its box clicks it.","files":null}]}